    body: 'Requires a first-class engineering degree and a valid GATE score in a related subject. Selection runs through GATE-score shortlisting, a descriptive exam, and an interview conducted by DRDO\'s Recruitment and Assessment Centre. Age limits sit around 28 for general category, with the usual relaxations for reserved categories.',
    note: 'A DRDO scientist role is research and design work, not a uniformed posting. It suits engineers who want mission-driven government work while staying in a lab or design environment.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Defence PSUs (HAL, BEL, BEML, MDL, GRSE) through GATE',
    body: 'These defence-manufacturing PSUs recruit engineers through GATE scores in a process that looks much closer to NTPC or ONGC recruitment than to a defence commission. Expect design, production, or systems-engineering roles inside aircraft, electronics, or shipbuilding manufacturing.',
    note: 'If you want defence-sector work without the uniformed commitment, this is usually the better-fitting door.',
