    q: 'Is the Short Service Commission (Technical) entry the same as the Technical Entry Scheme (TES)?',
    a: 'No. TES is a 10+2 entry route for students who have not yet started an engineering degree; the Army funds and runs their B.Tech training. SSC (Tech) is for engineering graduates or final-year students who already hold or are completing an engineering degree, with no written exam, an SSB interview, and commissioning as an officer after military training. If you have already finished or are finishing a B.Tech, SSC (Tech) is the relevant route, not TES.',
